<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vivi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vivi was the first station founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley">Henry Morton Stanley</a> in 1879 on the north bank of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>, opposite present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matadi">Matadi</a>, as the base for his work for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii">Leopold II</a>. It served as the first capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> until the administration moved downstream to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boma">Boma</a> in 1886.</p></div>
